WEBVTT

00:03:28.796 --> 00:03:31.236
three tonnes of carbon
into the atmosphere.

00:03:32.116 --> 00:03:35.356
But you want your trip to be net-zero.

00:03:36.396 --> 00:03:39.236
Well, today, you really have
three options.

00:03:39.236 --> 00:03:41.876
You could, of course,
simply decide not to go,

00:03:41.876 --> 00:03:43.996
in which case your trip
wouldn’t be net-zero,

00:03:43.996 --> 00:03:45.516
it would be absolute zero.

00:03:46.276 --> 00:03:48.916
Or you could decide
to continue on with your trip,

00:03:48.956 --> 00:03:52.556
but in this case, pay somebody,
on your behalf,

00:03:52.596 --> 00:03:57.396
to not emit three tonnes of carbon
that they otherwise would have.

00:03:58.316 --> 00:03:59.676
Now, in accounting parlance,

00:03:59.676 --> 00:04:02.556
this is what's called
an avoided emissions offset.